    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104876" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐγον-ία</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the third generation,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πονηρὸς ἐκ τριγονίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					58.17
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ἐκ τ. ὢν μυροπώλης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hyp.
					<u>Ath.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ Ἀθηναῖοί εἰσιν ἑκατέρωθεν ἐκ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					8.85
				</span></i>
			 citing <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
			</span></i> (who does not use the word in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ath.</u>
				55.3
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐκ τ.</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριγενείας</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> στιγματίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.446
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τ. βασιλεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					1.7.4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τ. παραμένειν, προελθεῖν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				11.10.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				12.2.11
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				4.131c
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριγένεια.</span></div>
